{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790375213,"nonce":"8w68i/ASPukW6DHOfbDOvEeXMCA=","title":"Lua: compile annotated functions on their declared types","message":"LuaLS annotations are registered by scope resolution (Scopes::declared) and read by exports, but the typer and the lowering ignore them: a function escaping to a host has `Any` parameters even when `---@param by integer` declares one, so every call through its record boxes and checks dynamically.\n\nThe declared types could seed the parameter types of an annotated function, with its record entry checking each argument the way the reference's C library does (`bad argument #1 to 'bump' (integer expected, got string)`), so the typed entry takes unboxed values. That changes what a call with a wrongly typed argument does (it raises rather than runs), so it wants a decision on whether annotations are a contract the compiler enforces or hints it may use with a guarded fallback.","files":null}]}